Let me look at the fuzz target more carefully and understand the exact vulnerability. The key issue is in `fuzz.cpp`:

```cpp
uint32_t hash_settings = *(const uint32_t*)data;
data += sizeof(uint32_t);
// ... settings ...
reader->parse(data_str, data_str + size, &root, nullptr);
```

The `size` is NOT decremented by 4 after reading the hash_settings. So `data_str + size` points 4 bytes past the actual end of the data buffer. This means the parser can read up to 4 bytes beyond the allocated buffer.

